// In the Int instance of `fib`, `<`, `-` and `+` resolve to the natives for two
// Ints, which the VM has instructions for, so the compiler writes those instead
// of calls: `n < 2` is the condition's `JumpIfNotLessI`, `n - 1` and `n - 2`
// are `SubIntI`, and the sum is `AddInt`. Only `fib` itself is called.
// compile: stdlib
fn fib(n) { if n < 2 { n } else { fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2) } }
fib(30);
